# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
tmp/
main
generated-app
bin/

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool
*.out

# Go workspace file
go.work

# Air temp files
tmp/

# Node (both directory and symlink forms — worktrees symlink node_modules)
node_modules
ui/dist/
# ui/build/ holds the UI bundle `bun run build` emits and main.go embeds
# via `//go:embed all:ui/build`. The bundle is a build artifact, so ignore
# its contents — but keep a tracked .gitkeep so the embed pattern always
# matches at least one file. Without it, a fresh clone (e.g. the validation
# pipeline cloning the hub before any UI build has run) fails go vet / go
# build / go test with "pattern all:ui/build: no matching files found".
# `bun run build` preserves .gitkeep across its clean step (ui/build.ts reads
# and restores it), so it never shows up as a deletion in a story commit.
ui/build/*
!ui/build/.gitkeep

# Playwright. test-results/ is unanchored so it's ignored at EVERY depth —
# Playwright writes it at the repo root (not just ui/) depending on which
# config + cwd the run uses, and a root-level test-results/.last-run.json was
# leaking into story commits.
ui/playwright-report/
test-results/
ui/test-results/
ui/.playwright/
ui/playwright/.auth/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Per-dispatch Ark MCP config — written fresh by ensureArkMCPConfig
# every time a Claude subprocess spawns and carries the absolute path
# of the running ark binary on this machine. Not portable, not for
# git. Ignoring keeps `git stash --include-untracked` from snapshotting
# it (which caused safeSnapshot/pull-loop conflicts when concurrent
# dispatches re-wrote the file between push and pop).
.claude/mcp-ark.json

# Same class, for the alternate-harness drivers (ARK_HARNESS): per-clone agent
# config written fresh per dispatch — opencode's .opencode/agent/ and root
# opencode.json, and codex's .codex/ (CODEX_HOME native
# state/auth; provider, dynamic doctrine, and MCP wiring are process-local).
# They carry clone-specific paths/IDs, so tracking them makes sibling
# clones conflict during parallel-build rebase/push (the auto-resolver can't
# merge a non-regenerable per-clone file). goose writes nothing to the tree, so
# needs no entry.
.opencode/
opencode.json
.codex/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Environment
.env
.env.local

# Journey-test local artifacts. journey-stack.ts captures the
# deliverable screenshot here, then shells out to
# `ark upload-artifact` to push the bytes to the orphan
# ark/state branch. The local copy is per-test scratch — never
# commit it to main (it'd land as untracked drift the workspace pull
# loop would race against, and the canonical artifact lives on the
# orphan branch already).
ui/tests/journey/.artifacts/
tests/journey/.artifacts/

# Runtime artifacts — SQLite databases written by `air`/the running app.
# These are per-instance runtime state and must not be committed: when
# regenerateAndAmend ran `git add -A` after a workspace pull, picking
# these up rewrote the merge commit's SHA and silently forked the
# workspace's main from the hub's main, breaking every subsequent pull.
app.db
app.db-shm
app.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal

# Ark build state (not application code)
.worktrees/

# .ark/ is scratch + sub-clone — agent clones, bare hub, feedback
# log, heartbeat files, the sub-clone working
# tree. All ignored on workspace main except the gate/models
# overrides, which are workspace-instance config and travel with
# the workspace across Ark sessions.
#
# .ark/state/ is intentionally NOT un-ignored on main — see
# ADR-0010. It is a SEPARATE git clone of the bare hub checked out
# on the orphan ark/state branch. Files inside it (stories/,
# _artifacts/, conversation/, releases/, context/, .git/) must
# stay invisible to workspace-main's `git add` so the workspace
# pull loop's divergence detector doesn't observe them as
# untracked drift.
#
# ADR-0010 Phase 5 lockdown is complete: every wizard-owned state
# surface (backlog + artifacts in Phase 1, conversation in Phase 2,
# releases in Phase 3, context in Phase 4) lives on the orphan
# ark/state branch. Workspace main cannot track those paths even
# by accident — `.ark/*` is unconditionally ignored except for the
# two static config files below.
#
# ADR-0010 also retires the legacy `.ark/backlog/` path — old
# workspaces with that layout are rejected with
# ErrPreMigrationWorkspace at OpenLogStore time.
.ark/*
!.ark/gate.json
!.ark/models.json
